review_comments:
This PR introduced several new unsafe code paths just so that a `ROS<byte>` could be smuggled as a `ROM<byte>` because that's what `ContentInfoAsn.Decode` expects. If this is going to be a continuing pattern, I'd prefer instead if we did something like this, which would keep all of the unsafe code contained to a single method:

```cs
internal ref struct ValueContentInfoAsn
{
    public string ContentType;
    public ReadOnlySpan<byte> Content;

    internal static ValueContentInfoAsn Decode(ref AsnValueReader reader, ROS<byte> span)
    {
        // move the unsafe PointerMemoryManager logic here
        // call ContentInfoAsn.Decode with the custom MemoryManager
        return /* ... */;
    }
}
```
